---
const proofItems = [
  {
    title: 'BetPanta Mobile',
    label: 'Public repo',
    stack: 'Next.js 16 / React 19 / Zustand / TanStack Query',
    href: 'https://github.com/loluskii/betpanta-mobile',
    description:
      'The clearest public frontend proof today. Mobile sportsbook product with routed home, live, sports, account, and my-bets flows plus visible betslip and realtime state infrastructure.',
    details: [
      'Shows frontend systems thinking around product shells, state, and reusable flows.',
      'Good source for future visual captures because real screens already exist in the app structure.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: '9jaDice',
    label: 'Public repo',
    stack: 'Nuxt / Vue / gaming UI',
    href: 'https://github.com/loluskii/9jadicev2',
    description:
      'A larger gaming-oriented codebase with visible product surfaces, promotional screens, auth flows, and multiple game content pages. Useful as proof of frontend product range.',
    details: [
      'Strong visual candidate for screenshots because the repo already includes product imagery and route surfaces.',
      'Supports the gaming and high-traffic product story from earlier work.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Next Backoffice',
    label: 'Public repo',
    stack: 'Next.js / admin workflows / operational UI',
    href: 'https://github.com/loluskii/next-backoffice',
    description:
      'Admin and backoffice proof covering dashboard, wallet, tickets, and settings surfaces. Less glamorous than consumer UI, but useful evidence of multi-role product work.',
    details: [
      'Supports the internal tooling and operator-side story from commercial work.',
      'A good source for screenshots showing data-heavy UI rather than marketing pages.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'FeedxNG',
    label: 'Public repo',
    stack: 'Nuxt / Laravel product story',
    href: 'https://github.com/loluskii/feedxng',
    description:
      'Better as a full-stack ownership case study than as a visual-first public repo, but still useful to back the marketplace and payments story once screenshots are added.',
    details: [
      'Supports the end-to-end build story from design through backend and payments.',
      'Will benefit most from recovered screenshots or archived product visuals.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<section class="services section" id="proof">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Public proof</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">What I can show in full right now.</h2>
      <p class="section-copy">
        These public repositories are the honest proof layer while private product screenshots are
        being restored. They are here to show real interface systems, real product structure, and
        real implementation range, not generic demos.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="proof-grid">
      {proofItems.map((item) => (
        <article class="proof-card card-surface">
          <div class="proof-card-top">
            <div>
              <p class="proof-label">{item.label}</p>
              <h3 class="proof-title">{item.title}</h3>
            </div>
            <a href={item.href} class="proof-link" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open repo</a>
          </div>

          <p class="proof-stack">{item.stack}</p>
          <p class="proof-description">{item.description}</p>

          <ul class="proof-list">
            {item.details.map((detail) => (
              <li>{detail}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="proof-note">
      <p>
        Next pass: replace some of these repo-led proof blocks with actual screenshots and route
        captures once the visual archive is assembled.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .services {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .proof-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 22px;
  }

  .proof-card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 24px;
    border-radius: 24px;
  }

  .proof-card-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .proof-label {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .proof-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .proof-link {
    min-height: 34px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .proof-stack {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .proof-description {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .proof-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    padding-left: 18px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .proof-list li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .proof-note {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .proof-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
